<title>HONG KONG: HK Nov retail sales up 8.0 pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Nov retail sales up 8.0 pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said on Friday Hong Kong's November retail sales totalled a provisional HK$18.4 billion, up eight percent on the year and down four percent on the month.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets:</p>
<p>						     Nov	Oct</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on-year)  - value    +8	+7</p>
<p>					 - volume   +3	+2</p>
<p>			  (on-month) - value    -4	+3</p>
<p>					 - volume   -5	+2</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on-year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +4	 +7</p>
<p>					 - volume  -5	 -2</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   +7	 -2</p>
<p>					 - volume  +7	 -3</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value  +13	 +6</p>
<p>					 - volume +12	 +6</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   +6	 +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  -1	 -3</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +11     +11</p>
<p>					 - volume   +5	+4</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value    -6	-4</p>
<p>					 - volume   **	-9</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value   +11     +26</p>
<p>					 - volume  +11     +25</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value    +3	+3</p>
<p>					 - volume   +0.2    +3</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
